.TH "VTTREGION" "3JS" "June 18, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
VTTRegion \- VTTRegion
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[CR]VTTRegion\f[R] interface of the WebVTT API describes a portion
of the video to render a \f[CR]VTTCue\f[R] onto.
.SH CONSTRUCTOR
.TP
\f[B]VTTRegion()\f[R]
Creates a new \f[CR]VTTRegion\f[R] object instance.
.SH INSTANCE PROPERTIES
.TP
\f[B]VTTRegion.id\f[R]
A string that identifies the region.
.TP
\f[B]VTTRegion.width\f[R]
Represents the width of the region, as a percentage of the video\(cqs
width.
.TP
\f[B]VTTRegion.lines\f[R]
Represents the height of the region, in number of lines.
.TP
\f[B]VTTRegion.regionAnchorX\f[R]
Represents the region anchor X offset, as a percentage of the
region\(cqs width.
.TP
\f[B]VTTRegion.regionAnchorY\f[R]
Represents the region anchor Y offset, as a percentage of the
region\(cqs height.
.TP
\f[B]VTTRegion.viewportAnchorX\f[R]
Represents the viewport anchor X offset, as a percentage of the
video\(cqs width.
.TP
\f[B]VTTRegion.viewportAnchorY\f[R]
Represents the viewport anchor Y offset, as a percentage of the
video\(cqs height.
.TP
\f[B]VTTRegion.scroll\f[R]
An enumerated value indicating how existing cues in the region move when
a new cue is added.
.SH EXAMPLES
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] region = \f[B]new\f[R] VTTRegion();
region.width = 50; \f[I]// Set the region to 50% of the video\(aqs width\f[R]
region.lines = 4; \f[I]// Render cues in 4 lines\f[R]
region.viewportAnchorX = 25; \f[I]// Place the region 25% from the left edge of the video\f[R]
\f[B]const\f[R] cue = \f[B]new\f[R] VTTCue(2, 3, \(dqCool text to be displayed\(dq);
cue.region = region; \f[I]// This cue will be drawn only within this region.\f[R]
.EE
